{"/":{"version":1,"title":"hashguard — Windows integrity checker","description":"Verify the Authenticode signature and SHA‑256 of every Windows executable, compare against a clean baseline, and spot files that aren’t what they claim to be.","keywords":"","h1":["Every file. Verified.","Scan something."],"h2":["Three checks. One honest verdict.","Point. Scan. Know.","Built for the terminal, too.","Four levels. No noise.","hashguard is not an antivirus. It tells you what changed and what doesn’t add up  so you know exactly where to look."],"h3":["Authenticode, verified the way Windows does it","Baselines","Heuristics","Fits how you work","Pick a folder","Every binary is checked","Read what stands out"],"h4":[],"h5":[],"h6":[],"p":["hashguard","Features","How it works","CLI","Levels","GitHub","VERIFYING SIGNATURES","CLEAN","kernel32.dll","Signed · Microsoft Windows","sha256 9f2c41…a7e0","DANGER","svchost.exe","System name found in \\Temp","sha256 c68b9f…02d1","WARNING","DMRCDecoder.dll","Certificate chain not built","sha256 401a67…b399","INFO","nvapi64.dll","Signed · NVIDIA Corporation","sha256 02ba49…ba55","hashguard checks the signature and SHA‑256 of every Windows executable, compares it with a clean baseline, and exposes anything that isn’t what it claims to be.","Download for Windows","Star on GitHub","Free & open source · MIT · Windows 10 and 11","WINVERIFYTRUST","AUTHENTICODE","SHA‑256","CATALOG SIGNATURES","BASELINES","HEURISTICS","RUST","TAURI","SVELTE","ZERO TELEMETRY","Measured on a stock Windows 11 install","6,210","binaries checked in one scan of System32","35 s","for the whole folder, on every CPU core","0","false “Danger” results on a clean system","What it checks","Each file goes through signature verification, a baseline comparison and a set of rules for the tricks malware actually uses.","WinVerifyTrust checks every embedded signature. Most system files have none of their own, so hashguard looks them up in the signed Windows catalogs too.","notepad.exe","→ embedded signature … none","→ catalog lookup ……… found","→ signer ………………… Microsoft Windows","✓ valid","Snapshot SHA‑256 hashes on a clean system. Later, see exactly what was modified, added or removed.","MODIFIED  drivers/netflt.sys","ADDED     tasks/updater.exe","REMOVED   —","svchost.exe in Temp. A “system” file signed by someone else. invoice.pdf.exe. The usual disguises, flagged.","✕  svchost.exe in Public","✕  invoice.pdf.exe","!  lsass.exe ← Evil Corp","Known‑bad hash blocklist","JSON export","Exit codes for CI","Parallel scanning","Desktop app + CLI","No telemetry","> hashguard scan D:\\Downloads --json > report.json","> echo $LASTEXITCODE","2   # danger found, fail the build","01","System32, Downloads, Program Files — or anything else on disk.","02","Hash, signature and catalog lookup for each .exe, .dll and .sys, in parallel.","03","A verdict per file, sorted worst first, with the reason spelled out.","","","","","","","","Command line","The same engine ships as hashguard.exe. Script it, pipe it to JSON, or fail a CI job with exit code 2 the moment something looks wrong.","PowerShell","> hashguard scan C:\\Windows\\System32","[ WARN ] DMRCDecoder.dll","certificate chain could not be built","[ INFO ] nvapi64.dll","signed by NVIDIA Corporation","6210 files scanned: 6008 ok, 200 info,","2 warnings, 0 danger","> hashguard verify C:\\Windows\\System32 -b clean.json","No changes against the baseline.","01 CLEAN","02 INFO","03 WARNING","04 DANGER","Severity","Clean","Valid signature, nothing unusual.","Info","Worth knowing — a third‑party signer in a system folder.","Warning","Unsigned where a signature is expected, or a broken certificate chain.","04","Danger","Modified after signing, masquerading as a system file, or on your blocklist.","EXPECTED","3f","9a","c1","07","5e","b2","d4","88","1a","e6","42","7d","f0","93","2b","c8","ACTUAL","e7","00684019  97df1c32  62d89c86  711092e8  01e886c6  a995fa85  40af754d  3ae6c9d5  b511cb8d  502aa28b  0e5df7ea  f6501c9